    "result_text": "The change is implemented and the test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nOn successful owner create, the app now enqueues a welcome notification via a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger. In `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. **Added the logger** (next to the existing `AUDIT` logger):\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger NOTIFY = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\n   ```\n\n2. **Called it in `addOwner`** right after the owner is saved and the audit event is emitted:\n   ```java\n   emitOwnerCreatedEvent(owner);\n   enqueueWelcomeNotification(owner);\n   ```\n\n3. **Added the helper**, emitting one line carrying both the owner id and the memberId:\n   ```java\n   private void enqueueWelcomeNotification(Owner owner) {\n       NOTIFY.info(\"Welcome notification queued: id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n   }\n   ```\n\nThe placement (after `clinicService.saveOwner`) ensures it only fires on a genuinely successful create, and after the memberId has been assigned. The idempotent-replay path returns early before this point, so no duplicate welcome is enqueued on retried requests.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes \u2014 the captured NOTIFY line (`Welcome notification queued: id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`) contains both the owner id and memberId.\n- Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
